110mDone\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m1\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;110m▾\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;243m├─▶ \u001b[38;5;110mbash\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252mls\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m-la;\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252mpython3\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m-m\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252munittest\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m2>&\u001b[38;5;252m1\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m|\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252mtail\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m-3;\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252mecho\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252m'--- stdlib check ---'\u001b[38;5;243m;\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252mgrep\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m-n\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;252m'^import\\|…\u001b[38;5;243m│ \u001b[39;48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;110m✓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;146;1mCreate shopping_list.py u…\u001b[39;22m \u001b[38;5;243m1m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;243m╰─▶ \u001b[38;5;110mbash\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243mrm -rf __pycache__ && \u001b[38;5;252mls\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;243m-la\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;243m└ \u001b[38;5;103mChange the target from 3 to 6. SHOPPING.md must include tea: buy 1, rice: buy 4, beans: buy 6. Add\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mtests for that corrected target.\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;243m└ \u001b[38;5;103mAlso reject negative quantities with a clear error, and preserve the last good SHOPPING.md when input\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;103mis invalid. Test that behavior.\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;243m└ \u001b[38;5;103mDocument the command to generate the report and run the tests in README.md.\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;243m▸ worked · ctrl+e\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;252mCreated shopping_list.py (stdlib only: csv, sys, pathlib) which reads ./pantry.csv and\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mwrites ./SHOPPING.md listing items below target 6 with buy counts; on invalid input\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m(missing file, malformed row, negative quantity) it prints \"error: ...\" to stderr, exits\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m1, and leaves the last good SHOPPING.md untouched. Added test_shopping_list.py with 13\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252munittest cases (parse, ordered target-6 report, negative/non-integer/header rejection,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mlast-good preservation, subprocess CLI exit codes) — all 13 pass. Documented the\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mgenerate and test commands in README.md. Evidence: \u001b[48;5;234mpython3 -m unittest\u001b[49m -> Ran 13 tests\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mOK; \u001b[48;5;234mpython3 shopping_list.py\u001b[49m on the checked-in pantry -> SHOPPING.md contains \"tea: buy\u001b[m\u001b[16X\u001b[32;106H\u001b[38;5;243m│ Next run setup\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m1\", \"rice: buy 4\", \"beans: buy 6\"; run with a negative quantity -> exit=1, \"error: line\u001b[m\u001b[16X\u001b[33;106H\u001b[38;5;243m│ Model · \u001b[38;5;252mdeepseek-v4.1-flash\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m2: quantity for rice is negative: -3\", md5 of SHOPPING.md unchanged (PRESERVED).\u001b[m\r\n "]
